# What git is not to look at, and nothing else.
#
# This file used to be the 430-line template from github/gitignore, of which eight rules ever fired —
# measured with `git status --ignored` and `git check-ignore -v` over everything currently on disk. The
# rest named tooling this repository does not use: Silverlight, BizTalk, ClickOnce, Chutzpah. A list that
# long is not caution, it is noise: nobody reads it, so nobody notices when something real is missing
# from it. What is here is what this repository actually produces, plus the editors it is actually opened
# in. Add a line when something new appears on disk, not in advance.

# Build output. `artifacts/` is where all of it goes; bin/ and obj/ remain for anything built outside the
# repository's own settings — a probe, a scratch project, an older checkout.
artifacts/
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Tt]est[Rr]esults/
*.binlog

# Packages, whether built here or restored into the tree.
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
/packages/

# The documentation site is built from docs/ by mkdocs; the output is never committed.
site/

# The browser build: the Firefox archive and the profiles it produces are artifacts, not sources.
/browser/out/
/browser/profile/
*.tar.xz

# Editors and their per-user state. None of it says anything about the project.
.idea/
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
*.suo
*.DotSettings.user
_ReSharper*/

# Whatever the operating system leaves behind.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Anything node touches, which here is only the browser runtime.
node_modules/
